  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is only 0.208, indicating RNA is the dominant signal and the primary avenue for improvement. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether the multiprofile structure (multiple profiles per cell with aggregation) provides meaningful additional information over a single profile, or whether the bottleneck is encoder quality. This experiment (config_002) tests the simplest logical extension of our best result: same RNA encoder (pca_n2000) but multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. It isolates the effect of profile structure and aggregation while holding the encoder constant, giving a clean comparison to config_001. If multiprofile+avgpool improves accuracy, it validates the direction and justifies testing transformer aggregation next (config_003). If it doesn't help, it redirects focus toward better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt). With 7 experiments remaining, this single-variable change is the most information-efficient next step to reduce uncertainty about the profile/aggregation axis before committing to more complex multimodal or encoder-swap experiments."
